  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "NEW\n\t\t\t* Either takes any number of alternatives: either.A()._.B().or.C()\n\t\t\t* Fix ends an either with what to do and why, for the failure to say: either.Empty().or.Fix(\"...\", because: \"...\")\n\t\t\t* Is().EqualTo(x) on every type, for equality within an either\n\t\t\tIMPROVED\n\t\t\t* A failed either names every alternative, not only the first\n\t\t\tFIXED\n\t\t\t* After a passing assertion, the one after and/but was skipped on numbers, objects, dates, bools and project graphs\n\t\t\t* Either-or works on strings and collections, and or is public\n\t\t\t* An either with no or passed silently; in a Spec it now fails at teardown",
